  "schema": "llm.mojo vocab-parallel LM head communication cost model",
  "produced_by": "Team V (zero/vocabparallel)",
  "date": "2026-07-27",
  "verdict": "NO at production shape",
  "provenance": {
    "all_volumes": "MODELLED - closed-form byte counts, no measurement input",
    "ratio": "MODELLED and BANDWIDTH-INDEPENDENT - both series move bytes over the same links by the same staged-copy mechanism, so any rate cancels",
    "milliseconds": "NOT INCLUDED in this file on purpose; ms requires a bandwidth anchor. See bandwidth_anchor below.",
    "bandwidth_anchor": {
      "value_gib_s_per_rank": 8.8,
      "status": "UNVERIFIED - derived from a prose docstring at llmm/zero.mojo:257-260 (~75 GB/s aggregate, ~92 ms for the full fp32 gradient allreduce at N=8). The repo contains NO reproducible collective-timing harness. Do NOT present as measured."
    },
    "charitable_model_note": "Every modelling choice bends TOWARD vocab-parallelism: per-collective latency/barrier costs are ignored (which penalises the small-volume side, i.e. overstates the benchmark-shape win, not the production-shape loss), and the extra B*T*C forward all-reduce required by a vocab-parallel ENCODER (Megatron-LM Sec 3) is omitted entirely. The option still loses 4.486x at production shape."
  },
  "constants": {
    "V_p": 50304,
    "C": 768,
    "L": 12,
    "max_T": 1024,
    "num_parameters": 124475904,
    "wte_elements": 38633472,
    "z3_embed_window_elements": 39421440,
    "note": "volumes are PER RANK, PER MICRO-STEP"
  },
  "formulas": {
    "micro_step": "one forward+backward over one micro-batch; ZeRO-2/3 bucketed reduce-scatter runs per micro-step (train_gpt2.mojo:4020-4024) and the wte all-gather runs per forward (train_gpt2.mojo:2582-2589), so both series share this cadence",
    "baseline": "2 * W * (N-1)/N   [all-gather z3 embed window + reduce-scatter its gradient]",
    "vocabparallel": "2 * (N-1) * B*T*C  +  3 * 2*(N-1)/N * N*B*T   [all-gather ln_f + reduce-scatter d_ln_f + 3 per-token all-reduces]",
    "breakeven": "N*B*T = V_p  (=50304 global tokens per micro-step); vocab-parallel wins strictly below",
    "caveats": [
      "Model is OPTIMISTIC for vocab-parallel: it omits the additional forward all-reduce of B*T*C that the vocab-parallel ENCODER requires (Megatron-LM Sec 3, 'an all-reduce (g operator) is required after the input embedding').",
      "Volumes are ring/reduce-scatter+all-gather equivalent, i.e. 2*(N-1)/N per all-reduce, matching this repo's hand-rolled staged-copy collectives (llmm/zero.mojo:236-264). No P2P on this box.",
      "Pure bandwidth terms; per-collective latency and barrier costs are NOT modelled. This penalises the SMALL-volume side, so the benchmark-shape win is overstated, not the production-shape loss."
    ]
  },
