  "steelman_grouped_vocab_parallel": {
    "description": "Partial vocab-parallelism: partition N ranks into G=N/g groups of g; split the vocabulary across the g members within a group and replicate across groups. g is a free parameter (g=1 is today, g=N is the extreme form). Evaluated so the rejection is not an artifact of only testing the extreme.",
    "formulas": {
      "activations": "2*(g-1)*B*T*C",
      "cross_group_dwte": "2*(G-1)/G * (wte/g)  -- every vocab row is owned by one rank in EVERY group, so its gradient must still be reduced across groups; vanishes only at g=N",
      "residency": "wte/g"
    },
    "finding": "At production shape TILING DOMINATES POINTWISE: for every g, tiling with t=g tiles reaches the identical residency wte/g at 1.00x communication, while grouped vocab-parallelism reaches it at 1.15x (g=2), 2.34x (g=4), 5.13x (g=8). No value of g is a good trade. Tiling also extends past t=N (16, 64 tiles) which vocab-parallelism cannot reach since g<=N.",
